# SSH allowed signers, consumed by `git verify-tag` in the release workflow.
#
# One line per signing identity, in the form:
#   <principal> <key-type> <public-key>
# for example:
#   chelsea@example.invalid ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nz...
#
# Public keys only. Nothing secret belongs in this file.
# The release workflow fails closed while this file lists no principal, which
# is the intended state until a signing key is recorded here.
